				{
					"name": "Refresh Token",
					"item": [
						{
							"name": "Login",
							"event": [
								{
									"listen": "test",
									"script": {
										"exec": [
											"if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
											"    var json = pm.response.json();",
											"    if (json.token) {",
											"        pm.collectionVariables.set('token', json.token);",
											"    }",
											"    if (json.refreshToken) {",
											"        pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', json.refreshToken);",
											"    }",
											"}"
										],
										"type": "text/javascript"
									}
								}
							],
							"request": {
								"method": "POST",
								"header": [
									{
										"key": "Content-Type",
										"value": "application/json",
										"type": "text"
									}
								],
								"body": {
									"mode": "raw",
									"raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"jdoe\",\n  \"password\": \"changeMeOptional\"\n}",
									"options": {
										"raw": {
											"language": "json"
										}
									}
								},
								"url": {
									"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
									"protocol": "http",
									"host": [
										"localhost"
									],
									"port": "9999",
									"path": [
										"api",
										"v1",
										"auth",
										"login"
									],
									"query": []
								},
								"description": "POST /auth/login — LoginRequest body (served at /api/v1/auth/login)\n\nOn 200 OK, saves `token` and `refreshToken` from the response into collection variables {{token}} and {{refreshToken}}.\n\nExpected response:\n```json\n{\n  \"token\": \"<jwt>\",\n  \"username\": \"jdoe\",\n  \"refreshToken\": \"<uuid>\"\n}\n```"
							}
						},
						{
							"name": "Refresh Access Token",
							"event": [
								{
									"listen": "test",
									"script": {
										"exec": [
											"if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
											"    var json = pm.response.json();",
											"    if (json.token) {",
											"        pm.collectionVariables.set('token', json.token);",
											"    }",
											"    if (json.refreshToken) {",
											"        pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', json.refreshToken);",
											"    }",
											"}"
										],
										"type": "text/javascript"
									}
								}
							],
							"request": {
								"method": "POST",
								"header": [
									{
										"key": "Content-Type",
										"value": "application/json",
										"type": "text"
									}
								],
								"body": {
									"mode": "raw",
									"raw": "{\n  \"refreshToken\": \"{{refreshToken}}\"\n}",
									"options": {
										"raw": {
											"language": "json"
										}
									}
								},
								"url": {
									"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh",
									"protocol": "http",
									"host": [
										"localhost"
									],
									"port": "9999",
									"path": [
										"api",
										"v1",
										"auth",
										"refresh"
									],
									"query": []
								},
								"description": "POST /auth/refresh — RefreshTokenRequest body (served at /api/v1/auth/refresh)\n\nPrerequisite: run **Refresh Token → Login** first so {{refreshToken}} is set.\n\nNo Authorization header required.\n\nOn 200 OK, rotates the refresh token and saves the new `token` and `refreshToken` into collection variables.\n\nExpected response:\n```json\n{\n  \"token\": \"<new-jwt>\",\n  \"username\": \"jdoe\",\n  \"refreshToken\": \"<new-uuid>\"\n}\n```\n\nExpected error (invalid/expired/reused token): 401 with message 'Invalid username or password'."
							}
						},
						{
							"name": "Get Current User",
							"request": {
								"method": "GET",
								"header": [
									{
										"key": "Authorization",
										"value": "Bearer {{token}}",
										"type": "text"
									}
								],
								"url": {
									"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/me",
									"protocol": "http",
									"host": [
										"localhost"
									],
									"port": "9999",
									"path": [
										"api",
										"v1",
										"auth",
										"me"
									],
									"query": []
								},
								"description": "GET /auth/me (served at /api/v1/auth/me)\n\nPrerequisite: run **Refresh Token → Login** or **Refresh Access Token** so {{token}} is set.\n\nUses the current access token from collection variable {{token}}.\n\nExpected response:\n```json\n{\n  \"username\": \"jdoe\"\n}\n```"
							}
						}
					]
				}
